# Nougat extraction stub — arXiv:1611.06946

**Status:** stub only. This replication ingested the paper via `pdftotext`
(see `work/paper.txt`, 807 lines, complete body + equations + tables in
plain-text form) rather than running Nougat. Nougat's advantage is
math-aware Markdown output; the replication tasks here (Stim circuit
construction, single-fault enumeration, Monte-Carlo LER scan) did not
require that level of structural extraction, so Nougat was not invoked.

**If a downstream consumer needs a Nougat Markdown extraction:** run
`nougat --model 0.1.0-base work/paper.pdf -o extraction/` on any free
endpoint (uicgpu has spare A100 for OCR-scale jobs per standing rule).
Expected wall ~1–2 min per page.

## Paper metadata

- **Title:** Fault-tolerant quantum error detection
- **Authors:** N. M. Linke, M. Gutiérrez, K. A. Landsman, C. Figgatt,
  S. Debnath, K. R. Brown, C. Monroe
- **arXiv:** 1611.06946v2 (May 2017)
- **Journal:** Science Advances 3, e1701074 (2017)
- **Code:** [[4,2,2]] Iceberg / Bacon-Shor sub-code
- **Platform:** 5 trapped 171Yb+ ions (4 data + 1 ancilla)
- **Stabilizers:** Sx = XXXX, Sz = ZZZZ
- **Logical operators:** Xa = X⊗I⊗X⊗I, Za = Z⊗Z⊗I⊗I, Xb = X⊗X⊗I⊗I,
  Zb = Z⊗I⊗Z⊗I
- **Headline claim:** La (FT logical) error < Lb (gauge) error and
  < bare physical qubit error over the tested range.

